# SuperConsole Plugin Specification
## How to build a plugin for the SuperConsole marketplace

A SuperConsole plugin is a folder in a GitHub repo with a `plugin.json` manifest
and asset files. When a user installs your plugin, SuperConsole fetches everything
declared in the manifest and configures it automatically.

---

## Folder Structure

```
your-plugin-repo/
  plugin.json              ← required: the manifest
  README.md                ← required: description for the marketplace

  skills/
    <skill-name>/
      SKILL.md             ← required: skill instructions
      README.md            ← optional: skill description

  commands/
    <command-name>.md      ← slash command files

  hooks/
    session-start.sh       ← runs when CLI session opens
    session-end.sh         ← runs when CLI session closes
    before-prompt.sh       ← runs before every LLM call
    before-mcp.sh          ← runs before MCP tool execution
    before-shell.sh        ← runs before shell command

  agents/
    <agent-name>/
      agent.md             ← agent definition file
      README.md            ← optional

  rules/
    <rule-name>.md         ← behavior rules injected into system prompt
```

**Example — Shopify plugin:**
```
shopify-plugin/
  plugin.json
  README.md
  skills/
    shopify-store-manager/
      SKILL.md
    shopify-product-writer/
      SKILL.md
  commands/
    check-orders.md
    update-products.md
    check-inventory.md
  agents/
    store-manager/
      agent.md
  hooks/
    session-end.sh
  rules/
    shopify-guidelines.md
```

**Example — Supabase plugin (multiple MCPs):**
```
supabase-plugin/
  plugin.json
  README.md
  skills/
    supabase-query/
      SKILL.md
    supabase-edge-functions/
      SKILL.md
  commands/
    query-table.md
    create-migration.md
    deploy-function.md
```

---

## `plugin.json` — Full Specification

```json
{
  "id": "shopify",
  "name": "Shopify",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Manage your Shopify store — products, orders, customers, inventory",
  "author": "SuperConsole",
  "icon": "🛍️",
  "category": "business",
  "scope": "project",
  "docs": "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/tree/main/shopify",
  "github_url": "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/tree/main/shopify",

  "skills": [
    "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/tree/main/shopify/skills/shopify-store-manager",
    "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/tree/main/shopify/skills/shopify-product-writer"
  ],

  "commands": [
    "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/blob/main/shopify/commands/check-orders.md",
    "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/blob/main/shopify/commands/update-products.md",
    "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/blob/main/shopify/commands/check-inventory.md"
  ],

  "agents": [
    "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/tree/main/shopify/agents/store-manager"
  ],

  "rules": [
    "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/blob/main/shopify/rules/shopify-guidelines.md"
  ],

  "hooks": [
    "https://github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins/blob/main/shopify/hooks/session-end.sh"
  ],

  "mcp": [
    {
      "id": "shopify-dev",
      "name": "Shopify Dev MCP",
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["@shopify/dev-mcp@latest"],
      "env": {
        "SHOPIFY_ACCESS_TOKEN": ""
      }
    }
  ],

  "connectors": [
    {
      "id": "shopify",
      "required": true
    }
  ]
}
```

