## catalog.json (repo root index)

The `SuperConsoleAI/plugins` repo must have a `catalog.json` at root.
SuperConsole app fetches this to populate the marketplace.

```json
[
  {
    "id": "shopify",
    "name": "Shopify",
    "description": "Manage your Shopify store",
    "category": "business",
    "featured": true,
    "icon": "🛍️",
    "path": "shopify/plugin.json",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "author": "SuperConsole",
    "install_count": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "supabase",
    "name": "Supabase",
    "description": "Full Supabase database and functions access",
    "category": "developer",
    "featured": true,
    "icon": "⚡",
    "path": "supabase/plugin.json",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "author": "SuperConsole",
    "install_count": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "google-workspace",
    "name": "Google Workspace",
    "description": "Gmail, Drive, Calendar access",
    "category": "productivity",
    "featured": false,
    "icon": "🔵",
    "path": "google-workspace/plugin.json",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "author": "SuperConsole",
    "install_count": 0
  }
]
```

---

## Scope Field

```
"scope": "project"   → installs to .superconsole/ in workspace
"scope": "account"   → installs to <app_data>/ machine-wide
"scope": "org"       → installs to <app_data>/ + org connectors
```

---

## Publishing to Marketplace

1. Fork `github.com/SuperConsoleAI/plugins`
2. Create folder: `plugins/<your-plugin-id>/`
3. Add `plugin.json` + asset files
4. Add entry to `catalog.json`
5. Open a Pull Request
6. SuperConsole team reviews + merges
7. Available in marketplace on next app sync

Or install privately by URL:
```
SuperConsole → Customize → Plugins → [+ Add from GitHub URL]
→ paste your repo URL → Install
```
